Fair point from my mate. The heart thing is what's really in my head, and I did go back to chips after a week, so I'm not going to pretend a label changes much. I don't read labels either, so honestly the picture on a bar is the most likely thing to get a glance, and the surgery ones are just telly-ad stuff I'd skip past. The bills are what decide what I buy, and a warning on a bar at the kiosk is not going to beat being skint or a bad day.

Still, I'd rather the dad thing sit closer to home than a cancer number, so C gets a bit more, and E drops because I don't think I'd actually notice it.

